>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Summary:</strong> OpenMDB collects no data. Your databases are opened, queried and exported on your Mac, and nothing is sent to us or anyone else.
  </div>

  <h2>What It Collects</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. There is no account, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. The app has no network access, so it cannot upload your databases.
  </p>

  <h2>What Stays on Your Mac</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your databases.</strong> OpenMDB reads only the files you open or drop on it and never changes them. Queries run on a temporary copy that is deleted when you close the database. Exported files are written only where you choose to save them.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    The one-time unlock is sold through the App Store. Apple handles the payment; we never see your payment details or Apple Account.
  </p>

  <h2>Sample Data</h2>
  <p>
    The bundled sample database comes from the Apache-2.0 licensed Jackcess test data. It is listed on the Acknowledgements screen in the app.
  </p>

  <h2>Not Affiliated</h2>
  <p>OpenMDB is not affiliated with Apple or Microsoft. Microsoft Access is a trademark of Microsoft Corporation.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions: <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com">matt@mattdonders.com</a></p>
